From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: XDG_DATA_DIRS and XDG_CONFIG_DIRS stay Unix-side

The session's search paths for Linux programs' data and settings (XDG_DATA_DIRS,
XDG_CONFIG_DIRS) do not exist on Windows, and a Windows build of GLib reads them as its own:
a Windows GTK program took SG's /etc/xdg/gtk-3.0/settings.ini (theme and icon theme
StainedGlass) and the Linux icon theme from /usr/share/icons, which it cannot load, and
stopped (Xournal++ 1.3.8: "Icon 'image-missing' not present in theme StainedGlass").
Like the toolkits' variables (5946) they are hidden from the Windows environment and passed
on to the Unix side of every child process. XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_DATA_HOME stay (shell32).
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -349,6 +349,22 @@
     return STARTS_WITH( var, "JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=" );
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: the session's search paths for Linux programs' data and settings (XDG_DATA_DIRS
+ * names /usr/share, XDG_CONFIG_DIRS /etc/xdg) do not exist on Windows. A Windows build of GLib reads
+ * them too, as Unix paths: a Windows GTK program took SG's own /etc/xdg/gtk-3.0/settings.ini (theme
+ * and icon theme "StainedGlass") and the Linux icon theme from /usr/share/icons, whose SVG icons it
+ * cannot load, and stopped ("Icon 'image-missing' not present in theme StainedGlass": Xournal++
+ * crashed at start). They stay Unix-side with the toolkits' below. The per-user XDG_CONFIG_HOME and
+ * XDG_DATA_HOME stay visible: Wine's own shell32 (user-dirs.dirs, the trash) reads them. */
+static BOOL is_xdg_search_env_var( const char *var )
+{
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_XDG_DIRS_VISIBLE
+    return FALSE;
+#endif
+    return (STARTS_WITH( var, "XDG_DATA_DIRS=" ) ||
+            STARTS_WITH( var, "XDG_CONFIG_DIRS=" ));
+}
+
 /* Stained Glass OS: the session tells Linux programs to draw on X11 (sg-common.sh, SG_LINUX_APP_ENV:
  * GDK_BACKEND=x11, SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11, ...). A Windows build of the same toolkit reads them too and
  * has no X11: Geany (GTK) said "cannot open display" and ended at once when started from Start or the
@@ -364,7 +380,8 @@
             STARTS_WITH( var, "GTK_" ) ||
             STARTS_WITH( var, "GSK_" ) ||
             STARTS_WITH( var, "SDL_" ) ||
-            is_java_env_var( var ));
+            is_java_env_var( var ) ||
+            is_xdg_search_env_var( var ));
 }
 
 static BOOL is_special_env_var( const char *var )
